popcorn source code is released under the MIT License, see LICENSE. This
repository contains no third-party source code. Unicorn and reflex are git
submodules under third_party/, pinned by commit. The other components below
are downloaded at build time from their upstream archives, pinned by version
and verified by sha256. Everything is compiled on the user's machine. The built
Python extension links Unicorn statically, so an installed popcorn extension is
a combined work subject to GPL-2.0-only.

Unicorn CPU emulator, popcorn fork at commit
722da2448374ab194fd0cafeeffceff368ce47ba, submodule third_party/unicorn
  https://github.com/Garcia6l20/unicorn, branch popcorn/v7m-special-reg-access
  Upstream: https://github.com/unicorn-engine/unicorn, commit 938efd13aeab
  plus one patch giving host access to M-profile special registers in any mode.
  The fork lists its changes, files and dates in POPCORN_CHANGES.
  License: GPL-2.0-only, see LICENSES/unicorn-COPYING. Parts derived from GLib
  are under LGPL-2.0, see LICENSES/unicorn-COPYING_GLIB. Built with the ARM
  target only and linked statically into the extension with hidden symbols.

reflex C++26 reflection library, submodule third_party/reflex
  https://github.com/Garcia6l20/reflex
  License: MIT. Header-only use.

nanobind
  https://github.com/wjakob/nanobind
  License: BSD-3-Clause. Its runtime is compiled into the extension.

robin-map
  https://github.com/Tessil/robin-map
